```

## Tool Use
```ts
const response = await anthropic.messages.create({
  model: "claude-opus-4-6",
  max_tokens: 1024,
  tools: [{
    name: "get_weather",
    description: "Get current weather for a location",
    input_schema: {
      type: "object",
      properties: {
        location: { type: "string", description: "City name" },
      },
      required: ["location"],
    },
  }],
  messages: [{ role: "user", content: "What's the weather in Paris?" }],
})
```

## Error Handling
```ts
try {
  const message = await anthropic.messages.create(...)
} catch (err) {
  if (err instanceof Anthropic.APIStatusError) {
    if (err.status === 429) // rate limited — exponential backoff
    if (err.status === 529) // overloaded — retry with backoff
  }
  throw err
}
```

## Token Management
- Set `max_tokens` explicitly — default may be too low
- Use `claude-haiku-4-5-20251001` for fast/cheap tasks, `claude-opus-4-6` for complex reasoning
- Monitor `usage.input_tokens` + `usage.output_tokens` for cost control

## Don'ts
- Don't hardcode the API key — use environment variables
- Don't use deprecated `claude-1` or `claude-2` models
- Don't ignore rate limit errors — implement exponential backoff
- Don't send unbounded conversation history — trim to control token costs
